+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-spc-001"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes its specialties the other way round: a page that lists every specialty it knows by its stored name, each with the veterinarians who hold it shown by full name — given name first, then family name. Every specialty appears together on one page rather than a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty does not appear at all; the page presents specialties and their holders, not the full veterinarian roster `[REQ-SPC-001]`.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name, all on one page.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given a specialty held by one or more veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each holder is shown by full name, given name before family name.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian does not appear.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given the directory, when it is opened, then it presents specialties and their holders rather than the full veterinarian roster.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. Specialties, and the veterinarians within each specialty, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+2. The page is reachable by its own address alone. This request adds no navigation entry and no link from another page, so it does not extend the navigation `REQ-SYS-001` requires; a visible entry point may follow as a later request.
+
+**Open question:** Whether "every specialty the clinic knows" is meant to include a specialty held by no veterinarian — shown with no holders — or only specialties at least one veterinarian holds. The seeded specialties are all held, so the two readings coincide today.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts) · **ADR:** [ADR: Specialty Directory Derived From Veterinarians](adr/2026-08-22-specialty-directory-derived-from-veterinarians.md)
+
 ### Language
 
 <a id="req-lang-001"></a><a id="req-lang-002"></a>
